 ('C1','Actual geometric application premises: C is nontrivially valued, complete and algebraically closed of characteristic zero and residue characteristic zero; V=C-degree-zero valuation ring. The given smooth projective curve and rational ample bundle have an ACTUAL proper flat finitely presented semistable a-adic formal model, with the given reference line bundle extending to it. A finite full-cycle skeleton is its dual metric graph, not a graph chosen independently of the curve. Every node has an actual formal neighbourhood with coordinates x,y satisfying xy=a_e≠0, and the smooth formal fibres are open discs. Loop edges can first be subdivided so the two branches meet distinct components. Adapted models containing every required finite set and dominating the reference model still need a complete proof; this record does not assert these premises from an abstract graph.'),
 ('C2','Choose a continuous PL function h on this actual skeleton, constant on the attached formal fibres, with a finite subdivision realized by the actual model. Assume edge lengths lie in Gamma_C=-log|C*|, vertex heights lie in Gamma_C, and slopes are rational. Let m be a common positive integer making mL an integral model bundle and every slope k_e=m slope_e(h) integral. Since Gamma_C is divisible, each m h(v) is still an actual value. Choose c_v∈C* with -log|c_v|=m h(v). On an oriented node annulus, t=-log|x| ranges from0 to ell_e=-log|a_e|; m(h(w)-h(v))=k_e ell_e.'),
 ('C3','On the smooth part U_v of each component choose the Cartier meromorphic equation g_v=c_v. On a node neighbourhood U_e choose g_e=c_v x^k_e. These are non-zero-divisors and are invertible on the generic fibre. On the v overlap x is a formal unit and g_e/g_v=x^k_e. On the w overlap, use xy=a_e to get g_e/g_w=(c_v a_e^k_e/c_w)y^-k_e. The scalar has absolute value exactly one by C2, so is a unit of V; y is a formal unit on this overlap. These ratios are units, including negative k_e. Ratios on all further overlaps satisfy the cocycle relation because they are actual ratios of the Cartier equations. Thus the equations define a GLOBAL vertical formal Cartier divisor D and O(D), with the canonical generic trivialization1. This is an explicit gluing construction, not a prescription of curvature on a graph.'),
 ('C4','In the local generator g_i^-1 of O(D), the canonical generic section1 has norm |g_i|. Its additive weight is -log|g_i|. Therefore the actual formal model metric on O(D), divided by m, is exactly h on each node annulus and the constant h(v) on every smooth formal fibre. Every formal unit has absolute value one on its generic fibre: both it and its inverse are bounded by one. Consequently the unit transition factors do not change the metric. Twisting the given model of mL by O(D) preserves the given generic algebraic bundle via that specified trivialization.'),
 ('C5','Compute degrees locally rather than assuming a slope-degree formula. On the normalization of component Y_v, the frame g_v^-1 gives a meromorphic section of O(D)|Y_v, regular and nonzero away from the nodes. Near an outgoing node it is x^k_e times the node generator, and x has a simple zero at that branch, so its order is k_e. At the opposite branch the order is -k_e, by C3. Thus deg(O(D)|Y_v)=sum_outgoing k_e, counting both branches of loops after subdivision. Since the residue field is algebraically closed, each node has degree one. Hence the divided component degree of the twisted model is theta_v+sum_outgoing slope_e(h)=theta_v+Delta h(v), in the Laplacian convention Delta=sum of outward derivatives. Total degree remains exactly V=deg L: edge contributions cancel, with no extension degree or additional factorial.'),
 ('C6','When every divided component degree in C5 is STRICTLY positive, the twisted compatible formal line bundle is fibre ample. Apply the reconstructed238 route, with its cutoff d0>=1, to the ACTUAL proper flat finitely presented reductions and this exact compatible bundle. Strong formal effectiveness algebraizes both carrier and bundle, and the original generic trivialization determines the same actual bundle through proper rigid GAGA. This use still requires checking all the actual model/completion/GAGA hypotheses; it is not an algebraization theorem for arbitrary metric graphs.'),
 ('C7','Relative ampleness over affine V gives a sufficiently divisible power globally generated by finitely many sections. Equivalently one can descend the proper flat ample finite-presentation pair to a Noetherian stage, use high-degree vanishing/base change there, and pull back. The resulting pure FS metric is the metric of the exact twisted bundle, by BE5.14. Thus the positive actual graph approximants, once C1-C6 are fully verified, are genuine same-bundle FS metrics. A limiting nef graph metric is recognized by uniform convergence of these genuine FS metrics; never infer FS recognition from nonnegative graph coefficients alone.'),
